edite the verification process.\n\n\nCross-referencing each entry, company names, registration numbers, and addresses are being validated against the designated databases. Investigating any discrepancies in company names or addresses to account for possible changes or errors. The process involves individual verification of each entry to ensure data accuracy.\n\nSubagent resources are being considered to expedite the validation procedure.\n\n\nValidating the first entry, I'm cross-referencing \"너스`\" with the provided registration number and address. A match confirms the initial data integrity; however, checking against additional databases is necessary to rule out possible discrepancies. Now validating the subsequent entry, I'll repeat the process of cross-referencing company name, registration number, and address. Each entry validation will be handled independently. Subagent resources may be engaged to expedite the remaining entries.\n\n\nConsidering a multi-pronged approach to deeply investigate the new company entries, focusing on business registration databases. Utilizing representative name and address searches, I plan to leverage available online resources for data retrieval. Representative name lookups will be performed to cross-reference business registration numbers and associated addresses.\n\nAddress searches will also be executed, looking for shared office spaces and co-located business registration numbers. Web crawling, including the use of an existing API, will be employed to automate the process of representative name lookups. The API will be used to retrieve registration details based on the provided representative names.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"node -e \"\nasync function test() {\n  const ceo = '기영주';\n  const url = 'https://bizno.net/%EB%8C%80%ED%91%9C%EC%9E%90%EC%A1%B0%ED%9A%8C/?query=' + encodeURIComponent(ceo);\n  const res = await fetch(url, { headers: { 'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0' } });\n  const html 